# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Recall V2 — project-specific. Strata is open source, but the RECALL
# LIBRARY is not: it is served from the hub and never committed or
# published. This repo carries the engine, not the library.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Backup copy of duplicate recalls — never commit
/recalls-duplicates-backup/

# Generated cache — none of it belongs in the repo.
#
# verified-recalls.json used to be re-included here as "the served-recall allowlist". It cannot be
# anymore: it is an id list plus a map of ids to paths under recalls/, and recalls/ is now excluded
# whole. In a fresh clone those 21 paths resolve to nothing, so loadVerifiedRecallsDirect() reads the
# file, fails on every entry with a "could not be read" line each, and only then falls back. A MISSING
# allowlist is the quiet path (it returns false immediately); a PRESENT-but-dangling one is the loud,
# confusing one. The hub's GET /v1/index is the public answer to "what does the library contain".
/cache/

# Build artefacts from `npm pack` — the published tarball is a release output, not source.
*.tgz

# >>> BEGIN generated recall exclusion — edit scripts/sync-gitignore.js, not this block
# The recall library is served from the hub and is NOT part of this repository. Everything under
# recalls/ stays local: the admitted recalls (their implementations are the project's actual IP)
# and the quarantined npm-scrape junkyard alike. No exceptions, no re-included paths — a single
# `!` line here would put an implementation on GitHub permanently.
/recalls/
# <<< END generated recall exclusion

# ── Local-only working directories (never in the public repo) ────────────────
# 496 MB of test artefacts from manual session runs.
/MANUAL TESTS/
# Scratch experiments and proof-of-concept spikes, superseded by recalls/ and strata/.
/poc/
/kickstart/
# Local task-runner state written into the user's own project during dev runs.
/strata/

# Scraped-corpus leftovers from the Recall era. Removed from history because
# data/local-patterns.json and the task-09 scratch file carry a live third-party
# Google API key that appeared as a hardcoded fallback in scraped source. Not ours
# to republish, private repo or not.
/data/local-patterns.json
/benchmark/task-09-rbac/

# ── NOT PART OF THE PRODUCT REPO ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repository is the MCP server, its benchmark evidence, and user-facing docs.
# Everything below is deliberately excluded:
#   - separate products with their own deploy (website, extension)
#   - the recall factory: scrapers, npm pipeline, autonomous authoring. This is the
#     methodology behind the library and is not shipped with it.
#   - internal strategy, roadmap and working notes
/website/
/extension/
/extension-landing/
/brandings/
/data/
/system/
/packages/
/server/
/tests/
/steps/
/Ideas/
