# ── BENCHMARK: publish the evidence, not the session records ──────────────────
# Only the current 60-run battery ships. Superseded experiments and raw agent
# transcripts are excluded: the transcripts carry host paths, session ids and full
# conversations, and the archived trees beside them are what the scores are
# actually computed from.
/benchmark/runs/*
!/benchmark/runs/exp-quality/
/benchmark/runs/exp-quality/**/*.log
/benchmark/task-*/

# Internal working notes — running logs, session findings, stale doctrine.
# docs/BENCHMARK.md is the published version of this material.
/STRATA-QUALITY-BENCH.md
/STRATA-BENCHMARK-FINDINGS.md
/STRATA-GATES.md

# ── MODULE SOURCE NEVER ENTERS THIS REPO ──────────────────────────────────────
# The product is the client. Modules live in the hub and are delivered to a user's
# project at call time; the library itself is never shipped or published. These
# paths are where delivered module source lands inside a benchmark output tree,
# and they were tracked once before — /recalls/ being ignored hid it from every
# check that only looked there.
/benchmark/task-*/
benchmark/runs/**/strata/lib.js
benchmark/runs/**/strata/selftest.js
benchmark/runs/**/strata/tests/
benchmark/runs/**/strata/composed-pkg/

# Brand assets exist for upload, not for the repo. The GitHub org avatar and the
# repo social preview are set once through the web UI — keeping the PNGs tracked
# afterwards just ships 90KB nobody reads. Regenerate with:
#   node scripts/render-banner-svg.js
/docs/assets/avatar-*.png
/docs/assets/social-preview.png
/docs/assets/wordmark.svg
